# i18n (internationalization)

**Language:** Locale **values** are user-facing copy in **English** (en-GB). Code, comments, and commit messages in **English**.

Single source of truth: **`src/global/locales/`** — wired in `ui/src/plugins/i18n.ts`.

## Official documentation

- [Vue I18n](https://vue-i18n.intlify.dev/)

## File layout

```
src/global/locales/
  index.ts              # exports { en }
  en/
    index.ts            # merges all domain modules into `en` object
    customer.ts         # domain keys
    order.ts
    errors.ts
    actions.ts
    pages.ts
    ...
```

- Add keys in the **domain file** that matches the feature (`customer.ts`, `enquiry.ts`, …)
- New domain module → create `en/{domain}.ts` and **import + spread** in `en/index.ts`
- Do **not** add locale files under `ui/` — only `src/global/locales/`

## Using i18n in Vue

```ts
import { useI18n } from 'vue-i18n';
import type { MessageSchema } from '@/plugins/i18n';

const { t } = useI18n<{ message: MessageSchema }>({ useScope: 'global' });
```

Or the project shorthand:

```ts
import { useAppI18n } from '@/composables';

const t = useAppI18n();
```

- Always type with **`MessageSchema`** — enables key autocomplete and catches typos
- User-facing strings in templates and scripts: **`t('key')`** — not hardcoded English in components
- Validation messages: `t('errors.fieldIsRequired', { name: t('name') })`

## Key naming conventions

| Pattern        | Example                                                | Use                 |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------- |
| Domain noun    | `t('customer.customer')`                               | Entity labels       |
| Nested object  | `t('order.status')`                                    | Grouped fields      |
| Shared actions | `t('actions.save')`, `t('actions.cancel')`             | Buttons             |
| CRUD helpers   | `t('crudItem.createItem', { name: t('fieldSet') })`    | Add/edit titles     |
| List titles    | `t('item.itemList', { name: t('customer.customer') })` | Grid/page headers   |
| Errors         | `t('errors.requireVehicle')`                           | Validation / toasts |
| Warnings       | `t('warnings.unSaveChangesWarningTitle')`              | SweetAlert copy     |
| Pages/menu     | `t('pages.diary')`                                     | Navigation labels   |

## Pluralization

Project uses pipe syntax in locale values:

```ts
customer: 'Customer| Customers',
```

In components: `t('customer.customer', 1)` / `t('customer.customer', 2)` or `t('template', 2)` for plural.

## Backend / shared copy

Locales are shared between frontend and can be referenced from backend-adjacent code. Keep domain boundaries — do not dump unrelated keys into `customer.ts`.

## Before finishing

- [ ] New user-facing strings added to `src/global/locales/en/` — not hardcoded in `.vue`
- [ ] New domain file registered in `en/index.ts`
- [ ] `useI18n<{ message: MessageSchema }>({ useScope: 'global' })` or `useAppI18n()`
- [ ] Reused labels use existing keys (`actions.*`, `errors.*`, `crudItem.*`) before adding duplicates
